    "role": "assistant",
    "type": "assistant_message",
    "content": "All 19 checklist items have been tested and recorded: **14 PASS, 5 FAIL**.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe application's core happy-path functionality is solid — dashboard creation/editing, filtering, live search, favorites, checklists, and persistence all work correctly. The failures cluster into two themes: **missing input validation** and **one unimplemented feature**.\n\n### Failures\n\n**CS-8 — No budget validation.** Saved budget `$55,000` was overwritten by `0` and then `-500`, both displayed verbatim (`$0`, `$-500`) with no error message and the dialog closing normally.\n\n**CS-9 — No guest-count validation.** Saved count `85` was overwritten by `-10` and by the fractional `12.5`, both accepted silently.\n\n**CS-11 — No wedding-date validation.** The past date `2020-01-15` replaced the saved future date `2027-09-04`. As a side effect the countdown element disappeared entirely, rather than being rejected.\n\n**IX-12 — Listing detail views are non-functional.** Both \"View Details\" (venues) and \"View Profile\" (vendors) do nothing: URL unchanged, zero dialog/modal elements in the DOM, and an unchanged page structure. This is a whole user-facing capability that is absent, not just a validation gap. Note the buttons carry `action=\"view-venue-details\"` / `view-vendor-profile` hints — a good reminder that semantic hints describe intent, not working behavior.\n\n**IX-19 — Cancel does not discard the draft.** The dashboard correctly kept its saved values, so this looks fine at a glance. But reopening the editor revealed the cancelled draft (`ZZZ`/`999`/`7`) still populating the fields. This is the most insidious of the five: the stale draft would be silently committed on any subsequent Save, so a user who cancels and later edits one unrelated field would unknowingly persist values they explicitly discarded.\n\n### Cross-cutting observation\n\nThe three validation failures share one root cause — the save handler performs no field validation whatsoever and writes raw input straight to state. Fixing that single handler would likely resolve CS-8, CS-9, and CS-11 together. IX-19 is adjacent, in the same dialog component: Cancel dismisses the dialog without resetting form state from the saved model.\n\nOne judgment call worth flagging: dashboard aggregate progress initially read `0%` while two tasks were complete. I did not fail this, because the app scopes aggregate progress to *saved* checklists — once I saved the checklist, it correctly showed `18%` (2 of 11), then `33%` (2 of 6) after unsaving the other. The behavior is self-consistent rather than buggy."
  }
}
